{
  "reasons": {
    "particle-exo": "Brenton adds a particle ('forth', 'away') to make a Greek verb English ('send forth', 'let go away'); the Greek verse has only the verb, which is the chunk before it, so the particle has no Greek word of its own (mw-u2w5klk.349.8).",
    "added-exo": "Brenton's English adds it to turn a Greek phrase into English (a noun or verb the Greek leaves understood: 'dry land' for ξηρόν, 'father' of 18:3, 'a time' of 8:9, 'own', 'one', 'come', 'go', 'way', 'part'), and each was read against its verse: no free Greek word renders it (mw-u2w5klk.349.8).",
    "pair-exo": "The Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word (6:7 ἐξαγαγὼν on 'out', 8:23 γῆς on 'Lord', 14:20 ὅλην on 'during', 15:17 κατηρτίσω on 'O', 18:16 διακρίνω on 'judgment', 19:21 διαμάρτυραι on 'solemnly'), which the model pass does not touch (mw-u2w5klk.349.8).",
    "other-verse-exo": "The Greek words are in the verse before or after, which has no chunk to point at: Exodus 6:17 ends with the English of the Greek verse 6:18's first words, 11:9 begins with the English of the Greek verse 11:8's last words ('Moses went forth from Pharao with wrath'), and 18:17 ends with the English of 18:18's first words (mw-u2w5klk.349.8)."
  },
